{# phone_mockup — a RENDERER-DRAWN smartphone frame showing a real social post (a
   "live social presence" element, the way Richard's NMR deck shows an "Insta
   Profil"/story in a phone). Pure CSS chrome (NO image of a phone) so it is crisp
   at print res and brand-agnostic: a dark device bezel + a notch + a white screen
   carrying an Instagram-style header (avatar + handle) over the real post photo.

   It NEVER fabricates engagement (no invented likes/caption text): it shows only
   REAL data passed in — the founder's real avatar, real handle, and a real post
   image. An optional caption line is shown only when real caption text is supplied.

   Token-only by construction: this macro emits ONLY structure; every colour / font
   / size lives in the `.c-phone` classes (styles/components.css), so the device
   stays brand-agnostic (the bezel is --color-ink, the screen --color-on-dark).

   photo_uri   the real post image (single-post mode's main content).
   avatar_uri  the founder's real avatar (small circle in the header). Optional.
   handle      the real account handle (shown as "@handle"). Optional.
   caption     OPTIONAL real caption text (shown only if supplied — never faked).
   posts       OPTIONAL list of real post image URIs → renders a PROFILE-GRID (a
               3-col grid of the real posts, the "active brand presence" look)
               instead of a single post. When given it takes precedence over
               photo_uri. Never fabricates follower/like counts — only real art. #}
{% macro phone_mockup(photo_uri='', avatar_uri='', handle='', caption='', posts=None) -%}
<div class="c-phone{% if posts %} c-phone--grid{% endif %}" aria-hidden="true">
  <span class="c-phone__notch"></span>
  <div class="c-phone__screen">
    {% if avatar_uri or handle %}
    <div class="c-phone__hdr">
      {% if avatar_uri %}<span class="c-phone__avatar" role="img" style="background-image:url('{{ avatar_uri }}');"></span>{% endif %}
      {% if handle %}<span class="c-phone__handle">@{{ handle }}</span>{% endif %}
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if posts %}
    <div class="c-phone__grid">
      {% for p in posts %}<span class="c-phone__cell" role="img" style="background-image:url('{{ p }}');"></span>{% endfor %}
    </div>
    {% else %}
    {% if photo_uri %}<span class="c-phone__photo" role="img" style="background-image:url('{{ photo_uri }}');"></span>{% endif %}
    {% if caption %}<div class="c-phone__cap">{{ caption }}</div>{% else %}<div class="c-phone__foot"></div>{% endif %}
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div>
{%- endmacro %}
